Blanks: {rule_id} the rule identifier used in expected-error annotations
1. Create test/{alias}.md exercising the rule with a config comment `<!-- markdownlint-configure-file {...} -->` at the end or start, marking each expected error line with `{{rule_id}:line}` after the offending text.
2. Create test/{alias}-default.md with default config verifying nothing is reported (disable unrelated rules via the configure comment where needed).
3. Create extra fixtures for edge cases (e.g. setext headings, unclosed blocks) as test/{alias}-<case>.md with annotated expected errors. (the rule has distinct edge cases worth covering)
4. Regenerate scenario snapshots with `npm run update-snapshots`.

